UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>What you will achieve</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>Upon completion of RII60520 – <strong>Advanced Diploma of Civil Construction Design in Australia</strong> (109181G) qualification,, students will be able to:</p><ul><li>Utilize computer-aided design (CAD) software such as AutoCAD and REVIT to create detailed drawings, plans, and designs for construction projects.</li><li>Apply project and risk management principles.</li><li>Prepare civil designs for various construction projects.</li><li>Manage civil works effectively.</li><li>Develop construction management skills that meet the demands of the Australian market.</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div><h4>Study Mode</h4><div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <p>The training will utilize a blended approach, comprising 15 hours of face-to-face instruction and 5 hours of supervised online study per week.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div><h4>Assessment Methods</h4><div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> Assessment methods for this course may include knowledge questions, <span>projects</span>, written reports, portfolios of work, assignments, case studies, self-assessment, observation, and role play. All assessments adhere to the Principles of Assessment (fairness, flexibility, validity, and reliability) and Rules of Evidence (validity, sufficiency, authenticity, and currency). </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div><h4>Course Structure</h4><div> <div> <p> </p><table><tbody><tr><td>CODE</td><td>Title</td><td>Core or Elective</td></tr><tr><td>BSBPMG531</td><td>Manage project time</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>RIICWD509E</td><td>Prepare detailed design of urban roads</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>BSBPMG533</td><td>Manage project cost</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>BSBPMG632</td><td>Manage program risk</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>RIICWD533E</td><td>Prepare detailed design of civil concrete structures</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>BSBTWK502</td><td>Manage team effectiveness</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>BSBWHS616</td><td>Apply safe design principles to control WHS risks</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>RIICWD507D</td><td>Prepare detailed geotechnical design</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>RIIQUA601E</td><td>Establish and maintain a quality system</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>RIICWD533E</td><td>Manage civil works design processes</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>RIICWD512E</td><td>Prepare Detailed Design of Motorways and Interchanges</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>RIICWD526E</td><td>Prepare detailed traffic analysis</td><td>Elective</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div><h4>Possible Career Outcomes</h4><div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> The units covered in the RII60520 – Advanced Diploma of Civil Construction Design in Australia (109181G) qualification provide individuals with significant experience in various career paths, including learning and development consultant, manager/head of department in a registered training organization (RTO), organizational learning and leadership manager, operational manager, workforce capability development leader, workforce planner, educational professional working within an RTO, and manager providing research or information related to <span> Career Development</span>. It’s important to note that the qualification description on the <a href="https://training.gov.au/">National Training Register</a> (www.training.gov.au) and/or https://www.myskills.gov.au/ provides this pathway information and does not guarantee employment or specific job roles upon completion of the course. </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div><h4>Credit Transfer</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>All credit transfer applications must be supported by <a href="https://asia.edu.au/details-student-orientation-information/">appropriate documentation</a>, such as a Nationally Recognised Qualification Certificate, Transcript, or Statement of Attainment. The documentation should correspond with the same qualification code, name, unit code, title, and duration as those included in the student’s application.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '104 weeks',
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Pre-requisites</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>There are no specific prerequisites stated in the training package for RII60520 – Advanced <strong>Diploma of Civil Construction Design qualification</strong></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div><h4>RTO Requirements for International students</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p><strong>International students applying for this course</strong>, whether onshore or offshore, must meet certain English language requirements. The requirements include being at least 18 years old and having completed the equivalent of Year 12. Additionally, an IELTS score of 6.0 is required (test results must be no more than 2 years old), although other English language tests such as PTE and TOEFL may be accepted. English language competence can also be demonstrated through evidence of being educated for 5 years in an English-speaking country or by successfully completing an English Placement Test.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div>',
    apply_form = 'https://asia.edu.au/advanced-diploma-of-civil-construction-design-rii60520/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '109181G';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>What you will achieve</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>Upon completion of the BSB80120 – <strong>Graduate Diploma of Management Learning in Australia</strong>, students will be able to:</p><ul><li>Utilize various techniques and tools to stimulate <span>creative and innovative thinking</span><br/>.</li><li>Plan, conduct, and report on applied research to influence strategic practices and outcomes within an organizational context.</li><li>Develop and implement coaching strategies systematically, monitor, review, and improve strategies to optimize learning outcomes for individuals and the organization.</li><li>Develop and maintain information processing systems to support decision making and optimize the use of knowledge and learning throughout the organization.</li><li>Plan, develop, implement, monitor, and evaluate a mentoring program that fosters learning through a defined and active learning partnership with a mentor.</li><li>Cultivate new and existing partnerships, establishing positive collaborative relationships within an organization.</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div><h4>Study Mode</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>The training will utilize a blended approach, comprising 15 hours of face-to-face instruction and 5 hours of supervised online study per week.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div><h4>Assessment Methods</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>Assessment methods for this program may include knowledge questions, projects, written reports, portfolios of work, assignments, case studies, self-assessment, observation, and role play. These assessments adhere to the Principles of Assessment (fairness, flexibility, validity, and reliability) and Rules of Evidence (validity, sufficiency, authenticity, and currency).</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div><h4>Course Structure</h4><div> <div> <table><thead><tr><td><strong>Code</strong></td><td><strong>Title </strong></td><td><strong>Core or Elective</strong></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>BSBCRT611</td><td>Apply critical thinking for complex problem solving</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>TAELED803</td><td>Implement improved learning practice</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>BSBHRM613</td><td>Contribute to the development of learning and development strategies</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>PSPMGT006</td><td>Develop a business case</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>BSBHRM611</td><td>Contribute to organisational performance development</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>BSBLDR601</td><td>Lead and manage organisational change</td><td>Elective</td></tr><tr><td>BSBLDR811</td><td>Lead strategic transformation</td><td>Core</td></tr><tr><td>BSBOPS601</td><td>Develop and implement business plans</td><td>Elective</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div><h4>Possible Career Outcomes</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>The units included in the BSB80120 – Graduate Diploma of Management (Learning) qualification are relevant to individuals with significant experience in various roles such as learning and development consultant, manager/head of department in a <strong>registered training organization</strong> (RTO), organizational learning and leadership manager, operational manager, workforce capability development leader, workforce planner, educational professional working within an RTO, and manager providing research or information related to career development.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div><h4>Credit Transfer</h4><div> <div> <div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><p>All Credit <a href="https://asia.edu.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/ASIA-Student-Application-Form-2024-V2-FINAL-1.pdf">Transfer Applications</a> must be supported by appropriate documentation, such as a Nationally Recognized Qualification Certificate, Transcript, or Statement of Attainment. These documents should correspond with the same qualification code, name, unit code, and title as those included in the student application, along with the date/duration of the <a href="https://asia.edu.au/courses/">course</a>.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div><h4>Additional Information about BSB80120 – Graduate Diploma of Management (Learning)</h4><div><div><p>For more details, Reach out to us at <a href="https://asia.edu.au/contact-us-astral-skills-institute-of-australia/">Astral Skills Institute of Australia</a></p></div></div>',
